meta {
  name: Communities - Is name available
  type: http
  seq: 122
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/is-name-available
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Knowledge Builders"
  }
}

docs {
  Whether a shared (private or public) community can take this name (#1136, ADR 0033). The answer is `data.available`. A name is taken when another shared community has the same name, whatever the case, or the address (slug) that this name gives. Personal communities never take a name.
}
